content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-102, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-19870, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal: steady drip at approximately 1 drop/second. No numerical allowable-leakage limit is supplied, so a numeric pass/fail comparison cannot be made. The applicable troubleshooting rule for leakage at the shaft seal is to replace the mechanical seal under procedure 5.2 and check alignment under 5.4.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration: 2.1 mm/s. Figure 3's HF-300 bearing-housing vibration-velocity scale applies; against its 0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A range, the reported value is within Zone A and 0.7 mm/s below the 2.8 Zone A/B boundary. It does not reach Zone C (4.5–7.1, restricted/plan maintenance) or Zone D (7.1–11.0, damage likely/stop the pump). Only the drive-end reading was reported, whereas weekly monitoring requires both housings and classification of the highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing temperature: 66 C. The bearing-housing temperature limits apply, and bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface. Normal operation is up to 70 C, so 66 C is within the normal range by 4 C; it is also 14 C below the 80 C alarm and 24 C below the 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The active seal leak requires planned corrective work, but neither reported condition-monitoring reading reaches a documented stop or trip threshold: vibration is below Zone D and temperature is below the 90 C trip. This supports P2 planned repair rather than an immediate shutdown; no leak-specific immediate-stop criterion is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical seal faces: investigate first for the isolated shaft-seal leak and confirm the seal-face condition when the seal is withdrawn.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal may have run dry. This is a listed probable cause of shaft-seal leakage; the pump uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is another listed probable cause. Check it under procedure 5.4; the reported vibration and temperature readings do not by themselves confirm or exclude misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Isolate and drain the pump before beginning mechanical-seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment; its mass is 68 kg. The back pull-out design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Remove the impeller nut and impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve HF3-455. Inspect the removed seal faces for wear or cracking and inspect the sleeve for scoring, recording the findings. Do not apply the service bulletin's 0.1 mm scoring-replacement threshold to this below-HF3-22000 serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. Fit one new HF3-450 component mechanical seal and one new HF3-120 casing gasket. Do not substitute HF3-450B: the supersession applies to serial HF3-22000 and above, while this pump must continue using HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. Reassemble and tighten fasteners to Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and M10 seal gland nuts to 25 Nm. Tighten M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm if those fasteners are disturbed. The 30 Nm bulletin torque is not applicable to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. Check shaft alignment as required for shaft-seal leakage. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "8. Before returning the pump to service, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in service; never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "9. Resume weekly condition monitoring by measuring vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classifying the highest reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type; correct replacement for serial HF3-19870 because the HF3-450B supersession applies only from serial HF3-22000.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit new during seal replacement and replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; do not manually lift the assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, per Table 6.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician, per Table 6, for the alignment check following the seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal selection: the manual parts list identifies HF3-450, while SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instructs pumps from serial HF3-22000 not to fit HF3-450 and to use HF3-450B instead. P-102 is serial HF3-19870, below that range, and the bulletin expressly says such pumps continue using HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Therefore HF3-450 applies to this work order.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque: manual Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts with lightly oiled threads, whereas the bulletin specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because HF3-450B and the bulletin serial range do not apply to HF3-19870, use 25 Nm, not 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve scoring criterion: manual procedure 5.2 requires inspection of sleeve HF3-455 but supplies no numerical rejection limit. The bulletin instruction to replace the sleeve when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm is within the instructions for pumps from serial HF3-22000, so it does not establish a limit for HF3-19870.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What mechanical-seal leakage rate, if any, is acceptable for this pump? The supplied evidence gives no numerical leakage limit against which to classify approximately 1 drop/second (C09).",
    "Was the reported 2.1 mm/s vibration measured as RMS as required by Figure 3, and what is the non-drive-end housing reading? Both housings must be measured and the highest reading classified (C06, C07).",
    "What sleeve scoring depth is found during disassembly, and what acceptance or replacement criterion applies to serial HF3-19870? The manual requires inspection, but the only numerical scoring threshold supplied is restricted to serial HF3-22000 and above (C10, C13).",
    "Has the seal ever run dry, and is the Plan 11 flush currently functioning correctly? Dry running is a possible cause of the leak, but the report provides no flush or dry-running history (C02, C09).",
    "Does installation of component seal HF3-450 require any seal-setting or sleeve measurement? No setting dimension is supplied, and the bulletin's pre-set/no-measurement statement applies to HF3-450B rather than HF3-450 (C10, C13)."
  ]
}
